# 7. USER INTERFACE AND EXPERIENCE

The interface must look like a premium sci-fi game.

It should not resemble a generic dashboard or an ordinary website.

Use a minimalist military-industrial interface with a dark translucent appearance and subtle lime-green accents.

### A. Main menu

Create a cinematic opening screen.

Include:

LAST SIGNAL

MISSION 01: THE LOST FACILITY

A short subtitle:

"Somewhere beyond the signal, something is waiting."

Buttons:

- NEW MISSION
- SETTINGS
- ABOUT

Use a cinematic background scene showing the rover and abandoned facility.

The main menu must be visually impressive.

### B. Mission briefing

Before starting the game, display a short briefing.

Example:

MISSION BRIEFING

LOCATION: RESEARCH SECTOR 07

STATUS: COMMUNICATION LOST

OBJECTIVE:
Recover three energy cores and restore the emergency transmission beacon.

Show a START MISSION button.

### C. In-game HUD

The HUD should contain:

Top left:
- Mission title.
- Current objective.
- Mission progress.

Top right:
- Mission timer.
- Health percentage.
- Vehicle speed.

Bottom left:
- Keyboard controls.
- Interaction hints.

Bottom center or right:
- Energy core collection progress.

Show interaction prompts contextually.

Example:

[ E ] COLLECT ENERGY CORE

When nearby.

### D. Pause menu

Implement a working pause menu.

Include:

- RESUME
- RESTART MISSION
- MAIN MENU

The game timer and gameplay must actually pause.

### E. Mission completion screen

Design a cinematic mission-completion screen.

Include:

MISSION COMPLETED

SIGNAL RESTORED

TIME TAKEN

ENERGY CORES RECOVERED

RESTART / MAIN MENU

All buttons must function.

