# 8. GAME ENVIRONMENT AND LEVEL DESIGN

Create a carefully designed compact level rather than randomly placing objects.

The level should contain several distinguishable areas.

### Zone A — Starting area

- Rover deployment position.
- Initial mission briefing location.
- Open terrain.
- Visible facility in the distance.

### Zone B — Industrial perimeter

- Damaged walls.
- Metal containers.
- Abandoned machinery.
- Rocks and debris.
- Warning lights.

### Zone C — Research facility

- Main industrial building.
- Entrance.
- Power equipment.
- First energy core.
- Environmental hazards.

### Zone D — Hazard zone

- Toxic gas area.
- Damaged equipment.
- Hazard warning indicators.
- Second energy core.

### Zone E — Communication sector

- Antenna structure.
- Emergency beacon.
- Third energy core.
- Final mission objective.

Place objectives strategically so the player must explore the level.

Provide clear visual landmarks and navigable paths.

Avoid spawning objects randomly in inaccessible locations.

