# 9. TECHNICAL ARCHITECTURE

Maintain a modular architecture.

Use the following structure as a guideline:

src/
  components/
    MainMenu.jsx
    MissionBriefing.jsx
    HUD.jsx
    PauseMenu.jsx
    GameOver.jsx
    MissionComplete.jsx
    LoadingScreen.jsx

  game/
    GameCanvas.jsx
    World.jsx
    Lighting.jsx
    Environment.jsx
    MissionManager.jsx
    CameraController.jsx

  entities/
    Rover.jsx
    RoverModel.jsx
    Collectible.jsx
    Hazard.jsx
    Beacon.jsx
    Building.jsx

  systems/
    VehicleController.js
    CollisionSystem.js
    MissionSystem.js

  store/
    gameStore.js

  hooks/
    useGameTimer.js
    useInteraction.js

  config/
    gameConfig.js
    assetConfig.js

  styles/
    global.css
    game.css
    ui.css

  App.jsx
  main.jsx

You may adjust the structure when technically justified.

### State management

Use Zustand for global state.

Centralize:

- Current game screen.
- Mission status.
- Health.
- Timer.
- Collection progress.
- Current objective.
- Pause status.
- Mission completion.

Do not use React state updates for every frame of movement.

Use refs and useFrame for high-frequency 3D operations.

Keep the UI responsive to meaningful game-state changes.

### Physics

Use React Three Rapier for collision handling where appropriate.

Implement:

- Ground collision.
- Rover collision.
- Environment obstacle collision.
- Collectible overlap detection.
- Hazard detection.
- Beacon interaction radius.

Avoid unnecessarily complicated physics.

The rover should have predictable and reliable controls.

### Performance

Optimize for a normal desktop PC and browser.

Implement:

- Reasonable polygon counts.
- Efficient materials.
- Shadow optimization.
- Controlled device pixel ratio.
- Reusable geometry.
- Instancing where appropriate.
- Efficient rendering.
- Resource cleanup.

Do not sacrifice the visual quality unnecessarily.

