These instructions are important.

- Actually write and modify the project files.
- Do not merely explain how to implement something.
- Do not stop after creating the project structure.
- Do not give me pseudocode in place of implementation.
- Do not ask me to manually create files that you can create yourself.
- Do not assume GLB assets exist.
- Implement sensible defaults wherever information is missing.
- Keep the source code modular and readable.
- Install dependencies when required.
- Run the development server and build checks.
- Fix the problems you discover.
- Keep me informed about important implementation decisions.
- When a feature depends on a missing external asset, implement a graceful placeholder and document what is needed.

Prioritize a functioning complete core game over a large collection of unfinished features.

If the full project is too large to complete in one execution, finish it in logical stages, preserving working functionality between stages.

